r the kid or  kissing for Paul Stanley my future is  like the last 10 or 15 years of my life  or 20 years of my life it's a story I  couldn't write better you know it is  something that I've worked at but it's  it is the American dream on all levels  the success I'm married to an incredible  woman  I have fabulous children and I have this  career doing what I did in school  because I loved it I played guitar in  bands when I was in junior high school  I'm still doing it today I am still  drawing guitars on paper only now  they're manufacture  you know now there's 13 million dollars  in sales of guitars that I draw life in  the future will be more of the same it's  um there's this great foundation that I  built that kiss is allowed that will  stand for anything that I choose to put  on top of it I'm just building this  monument but it's really a monument  maybe to the public so my life is really  about polishing the diamond you know  it's my life is a gem  so anything at this point is just a way  of making it Sparkle more whether it's  the next kiss album which is arguably  going to be the best album we've done  why because we're a band now of four  guys who get along great  who are geared towards making the band  great you can't succeed at your best by  saying how can the band make me more  successful you have to think how can I  make the band more successful what's  best for me will will play out when the  band is more successful is that  something that you knew when you started  out or did you have to learn that over  the years you learn that over time you  learn it the hard way I think you you  learn what a great partnership is and  what a great working relationship with a  band is to me a great working  relationship is based on knowing what  its limitations are if you don't expect  something from someone that they can't  give you you'll never be disappointed  the key to a great relationship is  keeping it realistic if you want  something that that partner can't give  you get it elsewhere spoken like a true  band leader of one of the most  successful bands in the history of the  world thank you so Mike you posh van Lee  from kiss thank you
 

